#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid "Panel"
msgstr "Panèl"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here you can configure the panel's overall appearance."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also have the icons themselves zoom out when the mouse is over them, "
"with the <guilabel>Enable icon zooming</guilabel> option. You can choose to "
"have tooltips appear when your mouse button is over an icon, by enabling the "
"<guilabel>Show tooltips</guilabel> option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid "Button Backgrounds"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &kde; panel supports so-called <guilabel>Button Backgrounds</guilabel>. "
"This means that the buttons shown on the panel will be drawn using "
"configurable images. To enable button backgrounds, simply choose the button "
"type from the list, and change the drop down box to the color image you "
"would like to use. Choose <guilabel>Default</guilabel> to return to an "
"unstyled button. If you choose <guilabel>Custom color</guilabel>, the color "
"button next to the drop down list will be enabled. Click on it to select a "
"custom color to use."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid "Panel Background"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Enable transparency</guilabel> to turn the entire panel "
"transparent. The desktop background will show through instead of a "
"background image or color."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There will still be small handles beside each applet, to allow you to "
"locate, move, and configure them. These can be turned off in the "
"<guilabel>Advanced Options</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you check <guilabel>Enable background image</guilabel> a picture will be "
"used to draw the panel's background, just as you can use a picture for the "
"desktop background. You can specify an image file in the line edit box below "
"or choose one by clicking on the <guibutton>Browse</guibutton> button. "
"You'll see a preview of the selected picture on the right."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The image can be tinted on-the-fly by enabling the option <guilabel>Colorize "
"to match the desktop color scheme</guilabel>. You might use a grayscale "
"texture that is tinted in this manner, to create a particular effect."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid "Advanced Options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Hide button size:</guilabel> option allows you to choose a "
"width in pixels for the hide buttons, if they are visible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The panel itself has several default sizes set, which you can switch between "
"by simply dragging the edge of it, or by &RMB; clicking on an empty space in "
"the panel, choosing <guisubmenu>Size</guisubmenu> and selecting the desired "
"size from the submenu. If you enable <guilabel>Allow Drag and Drop resizing "
"of panels</guilabel> then by choosing <guimenuitem>Custom</guimenuitem> in "
"the panel menu, you can drag the panel edge to any size you like."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Applet handles are normally visible beside each applet on the panel, so that "
"it is clear where to click to configure them, or to get to the panel menu. "
"You can instead have them <guilabel>Fade out</guilabel>, or hide unless you "
"hover the mouse over them, or you can choose to <guilabel>Hide</guilabel> "
"them completely."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Finally, if the panel is transparent, you can tint it with a color of your "
"choice. The slider allows you to choose how opaque the tint is. At the "
"lowest end, there is no tint visible, while at the highest, the panel is not "
"transparent at all."
msgstr ""

